From 7c8bd031189b91d1d5866fd2e72d1660513ec432 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 10:11:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(text): match native language parsing and formatting

Parse Bedrock language bytes before Java text conversion. Preserve native
ASCII key folding, value whitespace, escapes, NUL boundaries, duplicate
handling and raw UTF-8 identity. Keep parsed tables immutable and discard
their cache when the owned file changes.

Resolve exact keys before the native folded-key cache and retain whole
operation fallback, percent-token expansion and argument substitution.
Sequential arguments advance subsequent numeric references. Keep the
existing accepted English source policy; locale acquisition and language
selection remain separate work.

Use this engine in resource text and early disconnect/kick messages so
camel-case keys still resolve after native parser folding. Existing text
snapshots retain their tables when a content file is replaced.

Fresh original 1.26.51.1 execution verifies 1,099 file cases, 6,689 lookup
cases, five lookup-cache transitions, 752 formatter cases, 777 fallback
cases and 780 same-table parser/lookup/formatter compositions. The latter
supplies no translation lookup result. Ten focused checks pass; restoring
the old parser and three deliberate regressions fail behavioral assertions.

The probes declare their controlled raw inputs, language tables, argument
vectors, allocator/CRT and single-thread lock boundaries. They do not
establish full locale, asset-provider, client ownership or visible parity.

Keep shulker remainder lookup separate from language token expansion. The
native typed integer printf preserves embedded NUL and malformed bytes,
retains zero at precision zero, and honors sign flags on unsigned values.
Match the original formatter across 810 ordinary, boundary and precision
controls; keep unsupported Microsoft length extensions outside the grammar.
